title:: CaosMIDISlaveSync
summary:: MIDI clock slave tap: follows an external clock and transport.
categories:: CaosBox
related:: Classes/CaosMIDI, Classes/CaosSequencer, Classes/CaosBox

description::
Listens to MIDI clock (24 ppqn) from one input and adjusts
link::Classes/TempoClock:: so the CaosBox sequencer follows the external tempo.
The tempo is estimated from a window of 24 intervals (one beat), updated once
per beat and smoothed; the BPM value also reaches the GUI.

It follows the external transport:

list::
## Start: resets CaosBox to step 0 and plays.
## Stop: pauses CaosBox and keeps the step for Continue.
## Continue: resumes from the current step.
::

While the slave sync is attached, code::CaosSequencer.externalClock:: is true, so
the sequencer does not overwrite the tempo. `randomTime` is disabled and restored
when the sync is detached.

The usual entry point is link::Classes/CaosMIDI#-attachSlaveSync::. The input has
to be connected first: the CaosBox bootstrap calls code::connectAll::, otherwise
use code::CaosMIDI.connect:: before attaching.

classmethods::

method:: window
method:: minBpm
method:: maxBpm
Estimation window in intervals, and accepted BPM range.

method:: new
code::
s = CaosMIDISlaveSync(seq);                 // TempoClock.default, Main.elapsedTime
s = CaosMIDISlaveSync(seq, clock, timeFunc, transport);
::

instancemethods::

method:: install
Connects the MIDI clock, start, stop and continue responders to a source uid.
code::
s.install(src.uid);
::

method:: free
Frees the responders. It does not restore the sequencer; that is handled by
code::CaosMIDI.detachSlaveSync::.

method:: handleClock
Entry point for one clock tick. It can be called directly in tests.

method:: handleStart
method:: handleStop
method:: handleContinue
Transport handlers. They call the injected transport object, which defaults to
link::Classes/CaosBox::.

method:: seq
method:: clock
method:: transport
Read-only objects used by the tap.

method:: lastBpm
Last smoothed BPM estimate, or nil before the first update.
